17592186060837 #edb/ref 1061 639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060837 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83c1a05d-5319-54e1-9720-469dfe66522a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060837 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060838 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060838 #edb/ref 1061 642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060838 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "421e2979-c6df-5963-97d9-12da0c317f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060838 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060839 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060839 #edb/ref 1061 644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060839 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "51156115-46da-5b79-ab31-debdece8bd51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060839 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060840 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060840 #edb/ref 1061 645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060840 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e6bf63f-d0ed-582b-bfaa-01d712a200e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060840 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060841 #edb/ref 1061 647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060841 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23703e57-9d17-5cfe-bffc-b6497f55dc01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060841 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060949 #edb/ref 1064 "The **constant multiple rule** states that if a function $f(x)$ is multiplied by a *constant* factor $k$, then in order to differentiate $kf(x)$ we can take the derivative of $f(x)$ and then multiply by $k$ afterwards:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}\\left(k f(x)\\right) = k \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}\\left(f(x)\\right)\n$$\n\nFor example, to differentiate $y=6x^2$, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(6x^{2}) \\\\\n&= 6 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2}) \\\\\n&= 6 \\cdot 2x \\\\\n&= 12x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060949 #edb/ref 1065 345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060949 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "882aa12a-1be9-5fa0-8b2f-2a42007270f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060949 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060950 #edb/ref 1064 "The **sum rule** states that to differentiate the sum of two functions, we can take the sum of their respective derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(u(x) + v(x)) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} + \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nThe sum rule also applies to differences:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(u(x) - v(x)) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nAs an example, let's calculate the derivative of the function\n\n$$\ny = x^2 + x\n$$\n\nWe can apply the sum rule to find\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} + x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(x) \\\\\n&= 2x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060950 #edb/ref 1065 348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060950 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f81bca0f-c3d3-5653-b4d5-17a0d2af8863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060950 #edb/ref 1067 "The Sum Rule for Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235938 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235938 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235938 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "140ff256-58cb-520e-bd9f-ea7c8a886af9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235987 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235987 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235987 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b82390d-5224-5735-9b05-52d62582a7a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236246 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236246 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236246 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42c2e22e-7c41-5aba-866b-c2bfb66a3484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236558 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "76520e43-a300-5719-9281-b069c04cc15c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236726 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236726 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236726 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f7c3eb2-612e-5bea-9351-f3a4af8fd436" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186235938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186235987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186235938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237769 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fbea9dd8-14a2-537f-a32b-13a92d5ed3d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1071 "If $y=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},$ find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec04a0d1-192f-5dcf-aa4b-20bf3669c6e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237874 #edb/ref 1074 "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}=\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3/2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}){x}^{(-\\frac{3}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-5/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285562 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9{x}^{1/4}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285562 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285562 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5446db9d-f32b-503a-98c3-71bd4b13a940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285843 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9}{4\\sqrt[3]{x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285843 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285843 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "72b849ec-c73e-51c6-8bd6-7d57955bf8d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286135 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-9{x}^{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286135 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286135 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "93d4bb13-717f-50aa-afa5-f6147b1c9f75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286320 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{9{x}^{-1/4}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286320 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286320 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7da2020-89e3-5d5f-bbdb-6fb669e629c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286919 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9}{4\\sqrt[4]{x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286919 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286919 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9029ff2-9352-53d1-a4ea-86df802fa96d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186286919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287423 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8320dfd3-7a24-5485-a9b9-30a0c49ac165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494230 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494238 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494230 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494230 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $f(x) = 9x^{8}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494230 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15e2127d-c098-5e67-83ab-b40de632e719" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494230 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the constant multiple and power rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(9x^{8}) \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{8}) \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot 8x^{7} \\\\\n&= 72x^{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494234 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494243 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494234 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494234 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $f(x) = 10x^{4}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494234 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "399beb9c-d6e8-5212-8901-22851f54be48" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494234 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the constant multiple and power rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(10x^{4}) \\\\\n&= 10 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{4}) \\\\\n&= 10 \\cdot 4x^{3} \\\\\n&= 40x^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494256 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494247 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{35}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a18d304-5364-5f90-b5fc-66002ce43a5a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494247 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{35}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{6}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{35}{6}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494258 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494248 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b5ecd4a-071c-5b82-81cd-d8156d4440c5" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494248 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{6}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494228 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494249 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{32}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d2dda36-62f3-517d-9714-6527c6d15187" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494249 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{32}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{16}{3}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494253 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494226 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494253 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494253 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{28}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494253 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b4bba23-7243-55e3-8b30-b7d71a009323" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494253 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{28}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{14}{3}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494266 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494235 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494266 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494266 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $f(x) = 8x^{9}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494266 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d2107573-5dd9-5ec0-aece-60a9576c7d2f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494266 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the constant multiple and power rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begi